{
  "_comment": "Deterministic keyword routing rules. Single source of truth for both src/orchestrator/systems/keyword_router.rs and scripts/orchestrator_eval/keyword_router.py. Rules are ordered; the first whose route is still a candidate and whose required/forbidden terms match wins. All terms must be lowercase because matching runs on the normalized utterance. Rules are tuned for PRECISION, not coverage: an utterance no rule matches simply falls through to the embedding router, which is cheap, whereas a wrong keyword decision bypasses the similarity threshold and is executed unguarded.",

  "_interrogative_comment": "Markers of a read-only intent, not only grammatical questions. An utterance carrying one of these can never reach an edit route, which is the per-utterance form of Read Only mode.",
